Phase 7.1 - Improve compute tracing parallelism and eliminate serial density selection
  Depends on: Phase 7.
  Outcome: bounded density and lighting work exposes useful GPU parallelism without increasing
    ray counts, work budgets or changing the declared transport/integration model.
  [x] Record a narrow matched baseline for density selection, direct and diffuse tracing. Capture
      dispatch/group counts, occupied versus early-exit lanes, registers/spills, achieved occupancy,
      eligible warps and texture/memory stalls where tooling supports them. State GPU, settings,
      coverage, scene state and contention; distinguish measured limits from source-based suspicions.
  [x] Replace the single-invocation density queue merge/heap scan with parallel classification and
      bounded hierarchical selection. Reuse the lighting selector's established approach where useful
      without coupling the independent queue policies. Preserve initial-fill behavior, pending ages,
      persistent fair cursors, stable ties, exact selected sets, backlog and indirect arguments.
      Account for simultaneous scratch users and barriers; do not add CPU job-list readback.
  [x] Parallelize the eight independent diffuse gather directions per occupied voxel and combine their
      contributions through a bounded reduction. Preserve all eight directions, weights, recurrence,
      coherent old-field reads, finite checks and successful-only completion. Evaluate ray-to-lane
      mapping and reduction/register/shared-memory cost rather than merely increasing group size.
  [x] Emit separate solar/lunar direct lists and indirect counts so each compiled source dispatch
      contains only its own jobs. Preserve the shared 64 block-source budget and global fairness/
      priority selection, active-source handling, channel isolation and completion stamps. Empty or
      inactive source lists submit no tracing work; retain required ordering for shared RG texels.
  [x] Compare smaller workgroup shapes against the existing 256-thread tracing groups at identical
      selected voxel/ray counts. Adjust group-to-block indexing and indirect dimensions explicitly;
      measure occupancy, load balance, divergence and register pressure. Keep only measured useful
      layouts; neither maximum local size nor maximum occupancy alone establishes better performance.
  [x] Preserve deferred fence-gated status reads, drawing from isolated completed snapshots, bounded
      in-flight updates and dirty-block publication. Account for added reductions, dispatches, barriers,
      scratch and memory inside existing admission limits; do not restore render-thread GPU waits.
  [x] Use subagents for cached incremental builds and narrowly affected existing contract checks.
      Cover selection/fairness, unique source lists, reduction math, edge blocks and failure/publication
      only where changed; avoid redundant fixtures and approximation-quality/image/convergence gates.
      Reuse passing evidence; no routine clean build, full matrix or packaging. Final qualification
      remains Phase 9.
  [x] Repeat the same narrow measurements after each candidate, including total update cost and
      publication overhead. Record retained improvements and rejected variants honestly; update the
      proposal/current architecture for delivered scheduling and resource changes. Do not raise
      sampling budgets to hide poor utilization or claim hardware saturation from invocation counts.
  [x] Completion: serial density selection is removed, source-mismatched direct groups are eliminated,
      and diffuse-direction/workgroup choices have recorded cost evidence or explicit deferral with
      rationale. Queue, numerical and deferred-publication contracts remain intact; live frame-time
      and appearance acceptance remain separate qualification work.

Phase 7.1 verification
  Traceability: queue/fairness/scratch -> proposal / Metadata, budgets and source changes; ray lanes,
    recurrence/finite encoding -> Lighting, recurrence and encoding; fenced publication -> Nonblocking
    updates and drawable publication. Inherited ownership/units/enablement -> PBR.Clouds.md stored-volume
    sections, PBR.Atmosphere.Publication.md and Rendering.Enablement.md. Current docs reconcile layout,
    dispatch records and allowance: five private plus one shared density UBO, 48-byte lighting arguments,
    788 reserved bytes. No new candidate-sized storage, ray count, budget or approximation threshold.
  Delivered parallel density merge/cyclic prefixes/four-byte age threshold with stable ties; separate
    source lists preserve common completion/selection. Cooperative diffuse uses 256 threads, eight ray
    lanes per voxel and eight slices per block. Deferred status reads and isolated snapshots remain.
  RTX 4090 standalone timers, uncontrolled external contention: max 71,825-block metadata selector
    median 48.3727 ms baseline -> 0.2744 ms retained. A later repeat median was 0.4731 ms with samples
    0.2734/0.4731/0.7608; report variability rather than promising a fixed speedup or hardware saturation.
    Separate width20 authored tracing workload: guarded 55x66x55, uniform extinction .005, all occupied,
    64 direct jobs (32/source), 32 diffuse blocks/65,536 rays, old diffuse zero, unit sources/environment.
    Direct median 0.0532 ms -> 0.0532 ms; diffuse 0.2529 -> 0.0522 ms; transport plus coherent copy
    0.3133 -> 0.1024 ms. Dirty publication 0.0072 ms; transport/copy/publication bracket 0.1137 ms.
    These are separate coverage/brackets; do not sum them into a full-domain or live frame-time claim.
  Compared direct 256/128/64 threads: 0.0573/0.0553/0.0532 ms in the layout trial, too small a spread
    and no improvement over the old baseline to justify smaller groups. Diffuse cooperative256/128/64
    medians 0.0522/0.0584/0.0666 ms versus serial256 0.2499 ms. Retained256 for both; rejected production
    variants/branches removed. Register/spill/occupancy/eligible-warp/stall counters unavailable through
    the timer fixture; ray/group counts are source-derived, not measured occupancy.
  Complete candidate update: actual CloudVolumeSolution Poll/Submit with default detail/shadows/diffuse,
    width20, alternating native extinction .25/.2505, native heights +/-100m within the 800m band.
    Median sum 3.5308 ms across five callbacks/publication; samples 3.5308/2.9665/3.6844. Includes density
    validation/observation/generation/occupancy, queues, transport/completion, copy and publication.
    Startup/native upload/view/test fence waits excluded; callback submission gaps included. There is
    no matched old whole-update baseline. Live frame cost, appearance and full-domain costs remain later work.
