Phase 8 - Evaluate acceleration and update cost
  Depends on: Phases 7.4-7.7; Phase 1 initial acceleration decision.
  Outcome: a justified acceleration choice accounts for maintenance as well as traversal savings.
  [ ] Reuse the focused attribution and optimization evidence from Phases 7.3-7.7 for density,
      occupancy, direct, diffuse, copies and view costs, traversal/work counts and memory. Refresh only
      stale or missing cases needed for acceleration decisions; separate steady and changing content.
  [ ] Evaluate signed versus unsigned distance bounds and hybrid traversal against coarse DDA.
      Prototype only if the recorded feasibility/cost analysis warrants it; otherwise record explicit
      deferral and rationale without claiming a measured distance-field comparison.
  [ ] For any distance prototype, establish conservative distances to all potentially nonzero filtered
      density, accounting for anisotropic cells, quantization and reconstruction error. Do not use a
      visible isosurface threshold or assume hardware-interpolated distances are automatically safe.
  [ ] For any prototype, repair/revoke nonlocal certificates on density additions before publication;
      retain safe smaller bounds on removals. Fall back to safe DDA/no skipping during repair. Include
      recenter/domain changes, guards and all three ray consumers in the safety contract.
  [ ] Compare implemented alternatives including construction/update time, memory and weather backlog;
      preserve occupied integration semantics. Keep only the justified selected strategy and remove
      rejected experimental paths/resources. Do not require both structures in ordinary rendering.
  [ ] Carry forward Phase 7.6's diffuse-copy decision and costs. Reopen that design only if acceleration
      changes its hazards or measured cost; do not duplicate the completed comparison or silently
      introduce another publication scheme here.
  [ ] Verify affected conservative traversal/publication contracts with incremental checks; document
      the selected algorithm and distinguish analysis from measured results. No quality thresholds.
  [ ] Completion: selected acceleration has honest total-cost evidence and safe density-update semantics;
      all unimplemented alternatives are explicitly deferred, with no misleading comparison claim.

Phase 9 - Qualify the frozen candidate and reconcile documentation
  Depends on: Phase 8.
  Outcome: measured total cost, memory and user appearance determine candidate acceptance.
  [ ] Freeze the candidate and run canonical packaging/required final checks once. Verify delivered
      assets, selectable settings and cleanup; do not treat older candidate receipts as qualification.
  [ ] Measure total/per-pass GPU time and resident/peak memory at stated hardware/settings/resolution.
      Include startup, steady views, camera motion, wind, evolving weather, light transitions and
      recenter/replacement. Report update spikes, density/lighting backlog, age and fallback coverage.
  [ ] Compare matched view resolutions and label default-resolution differences. Separate illumination
      amortization from per-pixel view cost; disclose running-game contention and measurement limits.
  [ ] Obtain user-run appearance review for shape/thin layers, volume continuity, grid/seam motion,
      stable lighting, leakage, fallback transitions and stale-weather response. Never launch the
      game, invent acceptance, or replace review with automated approximation thresholds.
  [ ] Reconcile all proposal requirements and selected decisions with delivered code, documentation and
      focused evidence. Audit removable ownership and ensure no rejected prototype dependencies remain.
  [ ] Record acceptance or concrete outstanding limitations. If quality/memory/cost is unacceptable,
      retain candidate status and propose the next decision rather than silently shrinking coverage,
      adding procedural density or restoring a screen-space temporal dependency.
  [ ] Completion: package, correctness, GPU measurements and human appearance results are distinguished;
      all required acceptance is satisfied or explicitly left open. Do not remove/promote the older
      candidates without the user's separate replacement decision.

Final acceptance
  [ ] View, direct and diffuse consumers use the persistent 3D density and reusable lighting fields.
  [ ] Agreed memory/feature coverage, bounded updates, conservative traversal and lifecycle hold.
  [ ] User accepts appearance and measured total cost at the stated configuration; no FPS guarantee
      is inferred from architecture or headless tests.
  [ ] Proposal/current docs match implementation; outstanding work and deferred alternatives are explicit.
